\end{align*}
By setting $q=c'\log \left(\frac{Tn}{\delta}\right)$ for all $\delta \in (0,c_1)$ for constants $c'$ and $c_1 < 1$, we get $\ensuremath{\mathbb{P}} \left(W^2_{ti} \ge c'\log \left(\frac{Tn}{\delta}\right)\right) \le \frac{\delta}{Tn}$ and therefore, $\ensuremath{\mathbb{P}} \left(x^2_{ti} \le c'J^2(A^*)\log \left(\frac{Tn}{\delta}\right)\right) \ge 1-\frac{\delta}{Tn}$. Taking a union bound over $t \in [T]$ and $i \in [n]$ yields


